00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.375
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Does the
security of your applications

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:03.720
keep you awake at night?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.880
Stay tuned to learn
how Anthos can help.

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:08.814
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:11.620
Hi.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.680
I'm Priyanka, and
welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.630
Each of your
customers implicitly

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.420
trusts you with their
data, and keeping it secure

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.010
is your top priority.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.290
In this video, let's
learn more about

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.520
how Anthos makes it easier
to secure your applications.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.490
As key technologies like
containers and micro-services

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:33.460
become more commonplace,
traditional security models

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.960
are no longer sufficient.

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:38.140
Security posture is
fragmented based on parameters

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.440
like your platform-- do you
run on premises, or in cloud,

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.400
or both?

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:45.880
Your workloads, are you running
your VMs, or containers,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:46.960
or both?

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.800
Your services are they
regulated or sensitive workloads

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.840
or public-facing information?

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.360
Some problems with
older methods are

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.610
lack of visibility
into what is happening

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.890
on your networks,
lack of consistency

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:02.500
in terms of controls
or policies.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.170
Enabling a zero-trust
security posture

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.140
can help you solve these
issues and also modernize

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.500
your security for hybrid
and multi-cloud deployments.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.010
And Anthos equips you with
all you need to implement

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.230
a zero-trust model.

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.700
But first, what is zero-trust?

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.280
It is a security
principle that is

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.090
based on implementing security
controls at every single layer

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:27.580
of your stack and
with every interaction

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:31.690
or engagement, often
considered as defense in depth.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:35.680
This means you start with secure
bootstrapping at every node

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:37.460
and in every cluster.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.410
Next you secure the
network, not just

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:43.030
at the perimeter and the edge,
but by effectively segmenting

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:46.960
your deployment and securing
the network for each service.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:50.110
Then you secure access,
be it your infrastructure,

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.960
your application, or
the underlying data.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.690
You also secure your
deployments and rollouts

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.110
by making sure both your
code and your configuration

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:02.360
are only ruled out when
trusted and validated.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.500
And finally, you can't protect
against what you cannot see,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.039
so you need better observability
to enforce compliance

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:11.440
and quickly spot threats.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.740
Now let's see why you
need these and how Anthos

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:17.080
helps you accomplish these.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.000
First, secure bootstrapping.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.490
This is essential
because any issues here

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.100
can quickly affect
multiple services shared

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.760
in your infrastructure.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.020
Google Cloud provides you with
features such as shielded VMs,

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.710
container optimized OSs to
reduce your risk surface,

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:36.430
and encryption at rest to
prevent unauthorized access.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.860
You also have access
to hardening guides

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:42.670
to help you incorporate
best practices on premises.

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:45.970
Next, let's talk about securing
your network in such a way

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:49.190
that you are protecting
all your diverse workloads.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.760
This is where you can
protect against exfiltration

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.530
of your data, either
maliciously or unintentionally,

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.960
to uncontrolled environments,
unauthorized access

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:02.050
from the internet using
either stolen credentials

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:04.330
or by exploiting
misconfigurations,

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.800
and remote code execution
attack like SSRF.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:11.170
Google Cloud provides
you with everything

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.590
you need to protect both
your public-facing apps

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.320
and to seal your
perimeter using products

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.730
like Cloud Armor, Anthos GKE
security controls, and VPC

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:23.260
service controls.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.900
It is also essential
to secure access.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.140
This helps you protect against
unauthorized access using

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.860
stolen credentials, compromised
code in your deployments

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:37.030
through privileged escalations
or unpatched vulnerabilities,

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:40.600
malicious insiders with
access to internal endpoints,

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:43.680
and any underlying
network compromises.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.240
Anthos helps you implement
these controls using

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:48.790
a combination of features,
such as Anthos Service

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.580
Mesh to implement
authentication, authorization,

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.680
and encryption
between your services,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:57.700
and IAP to implement
granular access controls.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.030
We spoke about securing your
deployments and rollouts.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:03.010
This is essential
to reduce trust

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.590
on a single deployer or admin.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:07.480
Anthos provides you
with capabilities,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.410
such as binary authorization, to
ensure that your workloads are

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:14.440
trusted and validated
before they can make it

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:17.800
into your deployment,
preventing any untrusted code

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:19.190
from running there.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.399
And when it comes to
your configurations,

00:04:21.399 --> 00:04:24.760
Anthos Config Management
helps you establish a trusted

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.020
workflow, including reviews and
approvals for any configuration

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:31.810
changes that can impact
your deployments.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.080
This way, you can manage
your policy as code.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.860
In addition, monitoring is not
only key to quickly identifying

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:41.380
threats, but also to
maintain detailed audit

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.230
logs and records for compliance.

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:46.960
Anthos gives you access
to detailed audit logs

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.970
for your code, your
configurations,

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:51.060
and your network.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.500
So today we saw that Anthos
and Google Cloud give you

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.470
everything you need to
deploy a zero-trust model

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:59.030
for your applications.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.640
It gives you the ability
to deploy and maintain

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.040
a security posture
that is consistent

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.820
across in environments, policy
driven, optimized for cloud

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.190
native applications, application
and user context-aware.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:15.140
Try Anthos for yourself, and
get started on your journey

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:18.240
to zero-trust security
following the links below.

